    "durationMs": 423263,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built** (Rails 8.0.2 API-only, Ruby 3.4.3, PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL`):\n- `app/models/link.rb` — validates absolute http/https URL with host, code format `4-20` chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, generates unique 8-char codes\n- `app/controllers/links_controller.rb` — `POST /links` (201, 409 duplicate, 422 invalid), `GET /links` (ascending order with `total`), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic click increment via `increment!`)\n- `app/controllers/application_controller.rb` — JSON error bodies for 404/409/422 including malformed JSON\n- Migration with unique index on `code`; config reads `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials); `config.hosts.clear` so any test hostname works\n- `start.sh` — runs `db:prepare` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents it\n\n**Issues found and fixed along the way**: bundler resolved Rails to 8.0.5.2 (pinned to 8.0.2) and `json 3.1.0` broke Rails 8.0.2's encoder with `unknown keyword: quirks_mode` (pinned `json 2.9.1`); a generated code was accidentally an Array; duplicate codes returned 422 instead of 409 due to the uniqueness validation ordering.\n\n**Verification**: a 39-check curl suite covering every endpoint, status code, and error body passes 39/39, plus edge cases (empty-string code → 422, `null` code → generated, JSON body without Content-Type, non-hash JSON). I killed and restarted the server mid-test to confirm links and click counts persist across restarts. The links table is left empty and port 8000 is free for the test harness."
  }
